intention:
  name: "Games in tags with qg: (Godot 4)"
  version: "1.0.0"
  category: "game"
  goal: |
    Let a person write a whole 2D game — a platformer, a top-down adventure,
    a shooter, a fighting game, a board game — as tags, with no script of
    their own, and get a Godot 4 project that plays the same way every time
    from the same inputs, alone or with others over the network.

  principles:
    - "One schema (quantum/runtime/godot/schema.py) is the language: a tag, an attribute or a parent it does not list is a compile error naming the line"
    - "No escape hatch: text where statements go is refused ('a game is written in tags, not in script')"
    - "Deterministic: logic runs on the fixed physics tick (60 a second); the only random source is the scene's seed"
    - "What is only seen or heard (particles, camera, burst, shake, how a sound is played) never changes the game's state"
    - "Game state (q:set in q:application) survives scenes and goes into a save; scene state (q:set in qg:scene) is reset on entry"

  capabilities:
    - "Describe tiles, sprite sheets, sounds, particle effects, items and languages once, at the top of the game"
    - "Build scenes from tilemaps (CSV or Tiled), characters, prefab instances, zones, exits and spawners"
    - "Move the player with a ready-made controller, or compose one from parts"
    - "Give enemies a ready-made movement (ai=) or compose them from parts that seek, flee, keep their distance, patrol, wander, leap and shoot"
    - "React to touches, tiles, input, timers, deaths, animation ends, cursor clicks and menu buttons with actions and q: statements"
    - "Show a HUD, menus, dialogue and an inventory; save and continue; translate the texts"
    - "Play sounds and music, show particles, ease properties with tweens, frame the action with a camera"
    - "Play over the network in lockstep or with rollback, over ENet or WebSocket (a relay for browsers)"

  triggers:
    - '<q:application type="game">'
    - "qg:scene"
    - "qg:character"
    - "qg:prefab"
    - "qg:tilemap"
    - "a platformer, a top-down game, an arcade shooter, a fighting game, a board game"
    - "enemies, coins, keys, doors, levels, lives, a score"

  structure: |
    <q:application id="..." type="game">
      q:set ...                      game state
      qg:tileset / qg:spritesheet    pictures (qg:tile inside a tileset)
      qg:sound / qg:particles        what is heard and seen
      qg:item                        what the players carry
      qg:input / qg:multiplayer      keys, and players on other machines
      qg:language                    translations (qg:phrase and qg:asset inside)
      qg:prefab                      kinds of things (qg:state, qg:animation, qg:behavior, handlers inside)
      qg:scene                       screens; the first is where the game starts
    </q:application>

  semantics:
    # --- the game's resources, directly in q:application ---
    - "qg:tileset names a sheet of square tiles that tilemaps, sprites and prefabs draw from"
    - "qg:tile (in a qg:tileset) gives one tile a shape (x,y points or none), makes it one-way, or gives it a kind: ladder, water, ice or hurt; frames= and fps= animate it (water, lava, a torch: it and the frames after it in the row, in turn)"
    - "qg:spritesheet names a sheet of equal frames (24, or WxH) for characters and things; slice= (16, or left, top, right, bottom) makes its first frame a frame that stretches to a box, its edges as drawn (box= of a qg:dialogue or a qg:menu)"
    - "qg:input replaces the keys of an action (or declares a new one) for a player: keyboard, joypad and mouse names"
    - "qg:multiplayer makes the game networked for players= people in lockstep (delay=, check-every=), or with rollback=; start= is the scene play begins in; transport= is enet or websocket; min-players= lets the host start sooner with fewer (qg:start-now)"
    - "qg:sound names an .ogg or .wav; loop=true makes it music"
    - "qg:particles names an effect from a preset (puff, sparks, smoke, dust, fire, rain, snow, confetti, stars) with colour, amount, lifetime, speed and size"
    - "qg:language holds the game's texts in another language, one qg:phrase per text (text= as written, as= translated); font= is a font with the letters of its alphabet the game's fonts lack, which every text draws them from"
    - "qg:phrase is one translated text of a qg:language; a count's word (tr_n) has the forms its language has: one=, few=, many= (Russian, Ukrainian, Belarusian, Polish; one= and few= in Czech and Slovak), as= the rest"
    - "qg:asset (in a qg:language) is a picture or a sound of the game as it is in that language: name= a qg:spritesheet, qg:tileset or qg:sound, src= its file"
    - "qg:item declares something the players carry (a key, a gem, a heart): its picture, max=, start=, and the sound and particles of picking one up; held('name') reads how many"
    - "qg:prefab declares a kind of thing: sheet, frame, hitbox, tag (what collisions see), and how it moves with ai= (patrol, wander, chase, pathfind, fly, sway, shuttle, path, turret, behavior); solid=, one-way=, shape= make it a platform; gives= makes it a pickup; opens-with= makes it a lock; a fly prefab's walls=bounce turns off the tiles, trail= leaves a streak; spacing= keeps things of its tag apart; pushable= lets a grid walker's step push a solid one on (a crate); extends= makes it from another prefab, all of it but what it says itself; particles=, visible=, flip-v= and layer= are how it looks (a character has them too)"

    # --- what characters and prefabs are made of ---
    - "qg:state is a form of a character or prefab (small/big, calm/angry) with its own hitbox, frame, animations, speed and fire-every; qg:become switches to it; me.state reads it"
    - "qg:animation cycles frames=; idle, walk, jump, fall, walk-up, walk-down and attack play by themselves; loop=false plays once and runs qg:on-animation-end"
    - "qg:move is a fighter's attack on an action: frames, an active frame, a hit box (reach=, at=), damage, stun and push; holding away blocks"
    - "qg:behavior lists the parts a controller=behavior character, or an ai=behavior prefab, is made of"
    - "qg:gravity is a part: it falls and stands on floors (strength=, max-fall=); without it the body floats, top-down"
    - "qg:walk is a part: the keys set its speed across (axis=x) or in eight directions (axis=both), with accel="
    - "qg:jump is a part: a press on the floor leaps (height= or speed=), with coyote ticks, a buffer (a press just before landing), air jumps, a variable height and a cut"
    - "qg:keep-inside is a part: the scene's edges stop it"
    - "qg:wrap is a part: past an edge it comes back on the other side"
    - "qg:face is a part: the picture turns the way it moves (by=velocity) or is pushed (by=input)"
    - "qg:seek is an enemy's part: it goes for the nearest target it notices, around walls (way=around) or straight; sight=, through-walls=, speed=, when="
    - "qg:flee is an enemy's part: it runs straight away from the nearest one it notices"
    - "qg:keep-distance is an enemy's part: it stays between min= and max= pixels from the nearest one it notices"
    - "qg:patrol is an enemy's part: to and fro along a line, turning at walls and after distance= pixels"
    - "qg:wander is an enemy's part: a new heading every 30 to 90 ticks from the scene seed, and at once on bumping a wall"
    - "qg:leap is an enemy's part, with qg:gravity: it jumps at a wall (at-wall=) or while when= holds, at most once every every= ticks"
    - "qg:stand is an enemy's part: it stands still while its when= holds; the parts after it wait"
    - "qg:shoot is an enemy's part: it fires prefab= at the nearest target within range=, every every= ticks, whatever part moves it"
    - "an enemy made of parts moves by the first of seek, flee, keep-distance, patrol, wander and stand whose when= holds and that has something to do; me.doing names it"

    # --- what a scene holds ---
    - "qg:scene is a screen of the game: width, height, background, seed=, save=true to save on entering it as a room, y-sort=true to draw what stands lower in front, and ambient= a dark scene: the colour where no qg:light reaches"
    - "qg:tilemap is the level: CSV rows of tile numbers (0 empty, n is tile n-1, -n flipped) or a Tiled map (src=): its layers from one or more tilesets (each a qg:tileset with the same image), flipped and turned tiles, its objects placing prefabs (a state property), zones, exits and paths, and its own properties read by tiled('name'); collision=true makes its tiles solid; several are layers"
    - "qg:character is a body a player moves: controller= platformer, topdown, map, ship, fighter, grid, pointer (a grid walker its player's click walks by the shortest way) or behavior, with sheet, frame, x, y, hitbox and the controller's own settings"
    - "qg:instance places a prefab at x,y, with an optional name= and if="
    - "qg:cursor is a player's pointer (the mouse, or the direction keys by step=), snapped with grid=; qg:on-select reads it, and with id= it is read anywhere by its id (aim.x)"
    - "qg:path is a route of x,y points that ai=path prefabs spawned on it follow"
    - "qg:zone is an invisible tagged rectangle that runs on-collision handlers with that tag"
    - "qg:exit is a rectangle that leads to another scene (to=), arriving at that scene's exit named at="
    - "qg:spawner places count= instances of a prefab, one every every= ticks from from=, at x (or random), or along the edges heading inward"
    - "qg:sprite is a picture with no behaviour; its frame= may be an expression it follows tick by tick"
    - "qg:parallax is a backdrop that scrolls slower than the level (scroll=), repeated across"
    - "qg:emitter keeps a qg:particles effect going at a spot or across a width"
    - "qg:light is a glow of radius=, color=, energy= and flicker= at x,y of a scene, or on a character or a prefab (dx=, dy=: a lantern); shadows=true lets the solid tiles of a dark scene stop it: a wall lit, its shadow past it, and a wall opened lets it through; only seen"
    - "qg:map-node is a place on a world map; with scene= pressing jump there enters that scene"
    - "qg:map-path joins two map nodes both ways; requires= opens it only once that scene is in the game state cleared"
    - "qg:camera follows a character or the middle of several, with zoom, dead-zone, lead, smooth, and fit/zoom-min to keep several on screen; player= gives each player a view: on one machine the screen splits (side by side for two, quarters for three or four), over the network each machine shows its own player's"
    - "qg:music is the scene's looping music; scenes with other music crossfade (fade=), the same music plays on; in a handler it changes the music there and then (a boss's theme)"
    - "qg:hud is text over the game at a position, with a font and size"
    - "qg:counter (in qg:hud) shows a number: a q:set (bind=) or how many of an item are held (item=)"
    - "qg:icon in a qg:hud is a picture: a frame of a sheet (frame= may be an expression), the item after it on its line; color= on qg:text and qg:counter; if= and bottom-left, bottom-right on qg:hud"
    - "qg:text (in qg:hud) shows a string: a q:set (bind=) or an expression (value=)"
    - "qg:bar (in qg:hud) shows a number against its max: a q:set, or a fighter's id.health"
    - "qg:inventory (in qg:hud) shows the items held, each its picture and how many"
    - "qg:menu is a list of buttons, fields, sliders and keys a player moves through with up/down and chooses with select or a click; if= shows it only while true; columns= lays it out in a grid (left and right along a row), rows= shows so many rows and scrolls the rest into view; box= frames it with a qg:spritesheet with slice="
    - "qg:button (in qg:menu) runs what it holds when chosen; its label= may be an expression"
    - "qg:field (in qg:menu) is a text box bound to a string q:set; typing is local to the machine, and the keys type rather than play while it has them; shared=true makes it a draft that Enter sends with the player's input, so on that tick every machine sets the state and runs what the field holds, with sender and text (names, a chat); qg:menu local=true is the menu of whoever plays at this machine, of shared fields only"
    - "qg:slider in a qg:menu is a value left and right change while it has the focus: how loud a bus is (bus=, 0 to 100, kept between runs) or a number of the state (bind=, min=, max=, step=)"
    - "qg:rebind in a qg:menu shows an action's key; chosen, the next key, mouse button or joypad button pressed becomes the action's (Escape keeps it), kept between runs; local, like typing"
    - "qg:lobby is the ready-made networked-game menu: play here, host, an address, join, cancel; options= adds a button to the game's options scene"
    - "qg:dialogue is lines shown one at a time in a box; qg:say opens it and pauses the scene; speed= types each line in, sheet= is a qg:spritesheet of faces, box= a qg:spritesheet with slice= the box is framed with"
    - "qg:line is one line of a qg:dialogue: who= and text=, either may be an expression; portrait= a face beside it; qg:choice inside offers answers"

    # --- handlers: when something happens ---
    - "qg:on-collision (in a character or prefab) runs when it touches something of tag with=; side=top or bottom tells a stomp from a bump, left or right a side of the other; cooldown= spaces it out; me is the toucher, other what it touched"
    - "qg:on-tile (in a character) runs when it touches a tile of a kind; with cooldown= again while it still does"
    - "qg:on-hit (in a topdown character) runs when its swing reaches something of tag with="
    - "qg:on-fall (in a character) runs when it falls below the tilemap"
    - "qg:on-ko (in a fighter) runs when its health reaches 0; me the loser, other the winner"
    - "qg:on-damage (in a prefab) runs when it takes qg:damage and lives"
    - "qg:on-death (in a prefab) runs as its health reaches 0; in a scene with of=, when any thing of that tag dies"
    - "qg:on-locked (in a prefab with opens-with=) runs when a character bumps it without the item"
    - "qg:on-animation-end runs when a loop=false animation of the character or prefab has played to its last frame"
    - "qg:on-input (in a scene) runs when a player presses an action, or lets it go (on=release); sequence= (down, forward, punch) within= ticks and player= is a special move: the presses in order in that time, forward and back the way the player's character faces"
    - "qg:rumble shakes a player's joypad (and a phone in the hand) with strength= for seconds=: felt only, and over the network only on that player's machine"
    - "qg:on-separate (in a character or prefab) runs when it stops touching something of tag with= it touched; not when that thing is destroyed"
    - "qg:on-screen-exit (in a character or prefab, or in a scene with of= a tag) runs when it leaves the screen (the camera's view, or the scene), by side= any, top, bottom, left or right"
    - "qg:on-screen-enter runs when it comes onto the screen from outside it, by side="
    - "qg:on-select (in a scene) runs when a player presses select with their cursor somewhere; cursor and other (the thing under it) are in reach; action= makes another action choose (a qg:input with keys=MouseRight is a right click, WheelUp and WheelDown the wheel), and hovered() is the thing under a cursor at any time (hover)"
    - "qg:on-end (in a qg:dialogue) runs after its last line; in a qg:tween, when it is done, with me the thing it moved (a tween in it plays next: a sequence)"
    - "qg:timer (in a scene) runs after= ticks once, or every= ticks from from=, count= times"

    # --- actions: what a handler does ---
    - "qg:destroy removes a thing (other, me, or a q:set holding one)"
    - "qg:bounce throws the character up, as after a stomp (height=)"
    - "qg:damage takes amount= health from a thing (other, me, a parameter or a loop variable), moving or not; at 0 its qg:on-death runs and it goes"
    - "qg:respawn puts a character back at its start or last checkpoint, or a thing back where it was placed"
    - "qg:checkpoint makes where the other thing is the character's respawn point"
    - "qg:spawn places a new prefab at other, me, the cursor, the start of a path, or x,y, offset by dx,dy; heading=x,y (expressions) sends a flying one that way (at the pointer)"
    - "qg:swap replaces a thing with an instance of another prefab in its place"
    - "qg:become changes me or other to one of its states (qg:state)"
    - "qg:put moves a thing or character to x,y at once"
    - "qg:velocity sets the speed of a behavior character (a dash, a knock-back, a spring); parts go on from there"
    - "qg:deflect flips one axis of a flying thing's heading, or sets it to dx,dy"
    - "qg:tween eases x, y, rotation, scale, scale-x, scale-y (a squash), alpha or tint (a colour) to a value over seconds, with a curve, repeats and yoyo, in the game's ticks; its qg:on-end runs when it is done"
    - "qg:for-each runs what it holds once for every thing of tag= in the scene, var= naming each (damage every enemy near a bomb)"
    - "qg:time-scale runs the whole game slower or faster (scale=), for seconds= or until changed; each tick stays the same tick, so replays and peers agree"
    - "qg:quit closes the game (not in a browser: can_quit() says whether it would)"
    - "qg:after runs what it holds ticks= or seconds= later (a power-up that runs out, a fuse), with the names of its handler as they were; name= restarts one still waiting"
    - "qg:when in a scene runs its handler when condition= turns true (a wave beaten: count('enemy') == 0), read at the start of every tick, once until it has been false again"
    - "qg:start-now: the host starts the networked game with the players there, once min-players= are"
    - "qg:watch joins a networked game at an address with no seat, to watch it (catching up on it when it has begun); the lobby has a Watch button"
    - "qg:play-animation plays an animation of a thing or character from its first frame; name='' gives it its own animations back"
    - "qg:set-tile puts a tile in a cell of the tilemap or empties it; collision and pathfinding follow; tile_at(col, row) reads a cell"
    - "qg:play plays a qg:sound, with volume=, pitch= and vary=; directly in a scene, as it is entered; sounds= plays one of several each time (footsteps, bones); at= plays it from where a thing is, softer and to one side the farther from the middle of the screen, as a thing's own sounds are (a leap's, a shot's)"
    - "qg:stop stops a qg:sound; directly in a scene, as it is entered"
    - "qg:emit plays a qg:particles effect once where a thing is, or text= floats a number up from it (a damage number)"
    - "qg:beam draws a line between two things for seconds=, following them (a laser, a zap, an aiming line)"
    - "qg:label is text in the world, read every tick: over a character or a prefab (dx=, dy=), or at x,y of a scene"
    - "qg:steer is a part of a character's qg:behavior: left and right turn it, up pushes it the way it points (thrust=), it drifts and slows by drag=, up to max= (a ship, a car, a horse)"
    - "qg:camera-to sends the scene's qg:camera to a thing (target=) or a point (x=, y=), closer with zoom=, there in seconds=, for hold= seconds, and back to what it follows; the scene waits meanwhile unless pause=false (a lever shows the gate it opened)"
    - "qg:attach makes a thing carried by another (to=, me by default), dx,dy from it: it goes where the carrier goes and touches nothing (a key over a head, a torch in a hand); carrying(me, 'key') finds it"
    - "qg:detach puts a carried thing down where it is (target=, or from= and tag=): it touches again"
    - "qg:volume sets how loud a bus of the game's sounds is (bus=, value= 0 to 100), kept between runs; volume('music') reads it; qg:sound bus= puts a sound on a bus"
    - "qg:fullscreen fills the screen or goes back to a window (on=, or the other of what it is), kept between runs; fullscreen() reads it"
    - "qg:touch-button and qg:touch-stick (in q:application for every scene, or in a scene) press the game's actions on a touch screen, as keys would: a button its action= while touched, a stick left, right, up and down as far as it is pushed; show=always puts them on every device"
    - "qg:burst is a quick puff of particles where a thing is"
    - "qg:shake shakes the scene for frames= ticks"
    - "qg:give gives the players amount= of an item, up to its max"
    - "qg:take spends amount= of an item, not below 0"
    - "qg:reset-items starts the items over: every one back to its start=, the things picked up or opened back in place"
    - "qg:goto-scene leaves for another scene at the end of the tick (fade= from black); scene state is lost, game state stays"
    - "qg:say opens a qg:dialogue of the scene"
    - "qg:choice in a qg:line is an answer the player chooses (up, down, select): its label= (if= offers it only when true), and what it does, before the next line; a qg:say in it goes on in another dialogue"
    - "qg:pause stops the scene's characters, things, timers and spawners; menus, HUD and on-input go on"
    - "qg:resume goes on with a paused scene"
    - "qg:save saves the game state and a scene to come back to; has_save() tells whether there is one; slot= keeps several, a game each (has_save(2)), and the scenes with save=true save into the slot last used"
    - "qg:continue loads the saved game and goes on to its scene (slot= one of several)"
    - "qg:next-language shows the game in its next qg:language; the choice is kept"
    - "qg:host hosts the networked game on port=; this machine is player 1"
    - "qg:join joins at an address (host:port, or a relay's wss:// room); this machine is the next player"
    - "qg:leave leaves the networked game, or stops hosting or joining"

    # --- statements and expressions ---
    - "q:set in q:application is game state (saved=true keeps it between runs); in qg:scene, scene state; in a handler, an assignment with value="
    - "q:if, q:elseif and q:else choose between actions and statements in a handler"
    - "q:loop repeats a body over items= or from=/to=, with var="
    - "q:function (directly in a qg:scene, or in q:application for every scene and the prefabs) names a body of actions and statements; q:call runs it; q:return leaves it"
    - "expressions are written in braces and read state, me, other, cursor, the scene's characters by id (p1.health, hero.x), where a thing is (other.x, me.y) and the cell of the tilemap it stands in (other.col, me.row), what a body touched as it last moved (me.on_floor, me.on_wall, me.on_ceiling), and built-in functions; a field a thing does not have (hero.foo) is a compile error that lists the ones it has"
    - "functions: len, str, int, float, abs, min, max, round, floor, ceil, sqrt, random (from the scene seed), count, thing_at, tile_at (of a layer by name too), tiled (a property of the scene's Tiled map), carrying (what of a tag a thing carries), distance, nearest, sees, held, paused, talking, tr, tr_n (a count's word, one or other, in its language's form for n), language, has_save (of a slot too), volume (of a bus), fullscreen, net_status, net_players, net_player, url_param, can_quit, ticks (the scene's), sin, cos, atan2 (degrees), sort; pressing, pressed_for (ticks) and strength of an action, for player 1 or another"

  compilation:
    input: "<q:application type=\"game\"> with qg: tags and q: statements"
    output: "A Godot 4.4.1 project: project.godot, game.json, one .tscn and .gd per scene, addons/quantum/, the assets"
    pipeline: "QuantumParser (keeps app.xml_root) -> model.read_game (against schema.TAGS) -> compiler.compile_game -> Godot project"
    run: "quantum run game.q (--check opens it headless: any script error fails the build)"
    test: "quantum.runtime.godot_replay.replay(project, ticks, tape) returns the state after N ticks under an input tape"
